===== pr body =====
   1: # AI4DEV-60 â€” Sessions: expiry and revocation, refresh, and password reset
   2: 
   3: Deliverable D2 leaf L2 of the authentication requirement (`loop/decomp/req-001.md`, revision
   4: `0579425`): session expiry and revocation, automatic session refresh, password reset, and
   5: rejection of a wrong password.
   6: 
   7: **Acceptance ids this leaf owns:** AT-001.12, AT-001.13, AT-001.14, AT-001.38
   8: (`.taskmaster/docs/acceptance/at-req-001.md`). It builds on the accounts leaf, the GitHub leaf
   9: and the verification leaf (pull requests #47, #48 and #49), which landed signup, sign-in,
  10: account types and the email-verification flow this leaf's sessions sit on.
  11: 
  12: **Status: plan phase.** The plan is at `loop/items/AI4DEV-60/plan.md` and is under external
  13: review; code comes after the plan review is ruled. This body will be brought up to date as the
  14: item moves.
  15: 
  16: **The shape, in one paragraph.** Sessions are Supabase Auth's own machinery; this item ships no
  17: migration and no session table. The one shipped code change extracts the caller judgment from
  18: the edge plumbing into a pure module (`callerFromAuthAnswer` â€” fail closed on any non-2xx auth
  19: answer), so the judgment every deployed function runs on every authenticated request is
  20: type-checked and sits on the tested path. The fixture gains a clock-driven session mirror
  21: (issuance, expiry, revocation, refresh) and password-reset mirrors, each named in the fixture's
  22: mirror section with the live-proof check that binds it. The four acceptance tests go from
  23: declared-pending stubs to real bodies at the loop tier (13 green / 24 declared red for the
  24: requirement), and a live local-stack transcript carries the evidence the loop tier cannot
  25: reach: a revoked token refused by the real GoTrue and by a deployed function, an expired token
  26: refused and then refreshed without credentials, and the emailed reset flow end to end. Two
  27: retired acceptance ids (verification-link and reset-link lifetime semantics) stay deliberately
  28: unasserted.

