 121:     // second completion, and a malformed organisation name with messages written to be read by a
 122:     // caller â€” replacing them with "internal error" would throw away the only thing that says what
 123:     // to do differently. The status is 409 for anything the database judged and 502 for a transport
 124:     // failure, so a client can tell a refusal from an outage.
 125:     const status = outcome.status >= 400 && outcome.status < 500 ? 409 : 502;
